  <Document>
    <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 5, 2026 11:58AM EDT<br/><b>Next update:</b> Oct 5, 2026 5:58PM EDT</p><h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE (daily composite)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png?v=nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v5-2026-10-03" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), FIXED absolute scale <b>LOWEST 0.001</b> (dark blue) → 0.01 → 0.1 → <b>1.0</b> → <b>10 bloom</b> (red) → <b>HIGHEST+ 100</b> (deep purple). Each half-decade owns an equal share of the color; displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)<br/><a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html">https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 5, 2026 11:58AM EDT<br/><b>Next update:</b> Oct 5, 2026 5:58PM EDT</p><h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p>Chlorophyll-a concentration at the lake surface, a proxy for phytoplankton abundance/biomass. NOT a toxin measurement and NOT a harmful-algal-bloom diagnosis.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png?v=nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v5-2026-10-03" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), FIXED absolute scale <b>LOWEST 0.001</b> (dark blue) → 0.01 → 0.1 → <b>1.0</b> → <b>10 bloom</b> (red) → <b>HIGHEST+ 100</b> (deep purple). Each half-decade owns an equal share of the color; displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p><b>Units:</b> mg/m^3<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)<br/><b>Update:</b> daily composites<br/><b>Why high values turn red/purple:</b> Fixed absolute scale with anchors where lake water lives: background water spreads blue through green, active water reads yellow-orange, and only true blooms reach red-violet/deep-purple.<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html">ERDDAP dataset</a></p>]]></description>
